  q(ENT,'How should collected maggots be preserved for later measurement?','Hot water, then ethanol',['Freezing in tap water','Drying in the sun','Storing in a plastic bag'],'A','Hot water stretches the larvae to full length so their size can be measured.',BERT),
  q(ENT,'The predictable order in which insect groups arrive at a body is called:','Succession',['Migration','Pollination','Hibernation'],'B','Different insects colonize at different decomposition stages.',BERT),
  q(ENT,'Blowflies belong to which insect family?','Calliphoridae',['Formicidae','Apidae','Culicidae'],'C','Many blowflies have a metallic green or blue color and are often the first insects on a body.',BERT),
  q(BLOOD,'Which confirmatory test forms crystals when heme reacts with a reagent?','Takayama test',['Kastle-Meyer test','Luminol test','Marquis test'],'D','The crystal test confirms that a stain is blood, though not that it is human.',BERT),
  q(BLOOD,'Why can a presumptive blood test give a false positive with horseradish?','Plant peroxidases react',['It contains human DNA','It has red pigment','It contains iron cells'],'A','Presumptive tests must be confirmed because other substances can cause a color change.',BERT),
  q(BLOOD,'For an elongated bloodstain, where does the narrow tail point?','In the direction of travel',['Back toward the source','Straight up at the ceiling','Toward the closest wall'],'B','The rounded end shows where the drop first hit the surface, and the tail shows where it went next.',BERT),
  q(BLOOD,'A large amount of blood collects in one low spot around a body. What is this?','Pooling',['Cast-off','Spatter','Swipe'],'C','Pools can show how long a victim stayed in one place while bleeding.',BERT),
  q(BLOOD,'Which protein test helps confirm semen, even without sperm cells?','PSA (p30) test',['Amylase test','Precipitin test','Kastle-Meyer test'],'D','Prostate-specific antigen is useful when the suspect has had a vasectomy.',BERT),
  q(DNA,'How many alleles does a person usually have at each STR locus?','Two',['One','Four','Ten'],'A','One allele comes from each parent, and they may be the same or different.',BERT),
  q(DNA,'What is the graph that shows peaks for each STR allele called?','Electropherogram',['Chromatogram','Mass spectrogram','Histogram'],'B','Analysts read the peak positions to determine the allele numbers at each locus.',BERT),
  q(DNA,'What does a random match probability describe?','Chance an unrelated person matches',['Chance the lab made an error','Chance the suspect is guilty','Chance the DNA is degraded'],'C','Very small values make it unlikely that a random person would share the profile.',BERT),
  q(DNA,'Why are DNA samples taken from crime scene officers?','To rule out their DNA',['To charge them with crimes','To test their health','To add them to CODIS'],'D','Elimination samples show whether a profile came from staff instead of a suspect.',BERT),
  q(DNA,'Which group uses DNA testing to help free wrongly convicted people?','The Innocence Project',['The Body Farm','Interpol','The National Crime Lab'],'A','Many of its exonerations involved flawed eyewitness identification.',BERT),
  q(PSY,'What does a polygraph actually measure?','Body stress responses',['Thoughts in the brain','Truth directly','Blood alcohol level'],'B','Changes in heart rate, breathing and sweating are not proof of lying.',BELL),
  q(PSY,'Why are lineups run by an officer who does not know the suspect?','To avoid giving cues',['To save time','To scare the witness','To pick the right person'],'C','Double-blind lineups prevent unintentional hints that steer the witness.',BELL),
  q(PSY,'A hostage develops positive feelings toward the captor. What is this called?','Stockholm syndrome',['Munchausen syndrome','Capgras syndrome','Asperger syndrome'],'D','It is thought to be a survival response to fear and dependence.',BELL),
  q(PSY,'Which verdict finds a defendant responsible but also needing mental health treatment?','Guilty but mentally ill',['Not guilty by insanity','Mistrial','Acquittal'],'A','The defendant is held responsible but receives mental health treatment while serving the sentence.',BELL),
  q(PSY,'A crime scene is chaotic, with a weapon from the scene left behind. Which offender type is suggested?','Disorganized offender',['Organized offender','Professional thief','Contract killer'],'B','These offenders act impulsively and often live near the crime scene.',BELL)
